        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">Average technology\n\n# Included processes\nThis data set includes the material use for the manufacturing of the electronic installations in an office building according to Klingler and Kasser, 2011. The source states that 95 % of the mass volume is accounted for, which covers about 100 individual components. 1 office building was taken into account. The energy reference area is 2062 m2 for the basic construction and 1405 m2 for the tenant equipment (Mieterausbau). Basic and tenant"s equipment were taken into account both relative to each energy reference areas. The neon tubes and lamp fitting, as well as the control gear (EVG and VVG) were modelled with an energy saving light bulb. The electrical system has a life-span of 30 years. Transport is included.</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
